  "id": "competition-tolerance",
  "term": "competition tolerance",
  "definition": "Competition tolerance is a response in which an established competitor changes to a slower, more resource-efficient way of growing so it places less pressure on a rival for shared nutrients. In the source, this is described as an alternative to moving away or switching to different resources.",
